Evolution of Mobile Phones to Smartphones (Nokia to iPhone) 

The evolution of mobile phones from Nokia devices to the iPhone represents a significant milestone in mobile and portable computing. Initially, mobile phones were mainly used for making calls and sending text messages 

 

. Nokia became a leading mobile phone brand because of its durable designs, reliable performance, and long battery life. 

 However, technological advancements gradually transformed mobile phones into powerful devices capable of performing many different tasks. 

The introduction of smartphones changed how people communicate and interact with technology. 

 

 Apple's first iPhone, launched in 2007, popularized a touchscreen-based design that combined communication, internet browsing, music and photography in one device. Although Nokia had developed advanced mobile phones before this, the iPhone helped establish a new direction for mobile computing through its intuitive interface and application-based ecosystem. 

 

 This encouraged other manufacturers to develop increasingly advanced smartphones. 

 
